  "id": "DrugBank_DB00268 - MONDO_10482",
  "verbalization": "Ropinirole is implicated in the pathogenesis of X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome through its association with Parkinson Disease, which in turn is linked to the syndrome via multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Ropinirole may exert a therapeutic effect on this condition by modulating dopaminergic pathways, as it is indicated for Parkinson Disease and is linked to the syndrome through its interaction with other drugs such as Istradefylline, Tolcapone, and Rotigotine. These drugs are known to target different aspects of Parkinson Disease, including dopamine receptor activation and neuroprotection, which may contribute to the management of X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome. The overlapping indications and the shared pathogenic mechanisms highlight a potential role for Ropinirole in this syndrome, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
